## Scenario 3 — Gameplay Interaction

### Phase 14: Backend — Data Model
- [x] T14.1 Add `Guess` interface to `backend/src/models/game.ts` (`{ id, participantId, participantName, text, correct, submittedAt }`)
- [x] T14.2 Add `scores: Record<string, number>` and `guesses: Guess[]` to `Room` interface
- [x] T14.3 Add `scores: Record<string, number>` and `guesses: Guess[]` to `RoomSnapshot` interface

### Phase 15: Backend — Service & API
- [x] T15.1 Initialise `scores` and `guesses` as empty structures in `createRoom` and `startGame`
- [x] T15.2 Add `submitGuess(code, participantId, guessText)` in `backend/src/services/roomStore.ts`
  - [x] Trim the guess; reject if empty (throw Error)
  - [x] Look up secret word; compare case-insensitively
  - [x] If correct, add 100 to `scores[participantId]`
  - [x] Push the `Guess` record to `room.guesses`
- [x] T15.3 Expose `guesses` and `scores` in `toRoomSnapshot`
- [x] T15.4 Add `guessSchema` Zod schema in `backend/src/api/schemas.ts`
- [x] T15.5 Add `POST /rooms/:code/guess` endpoint in `backend/src/api/rooms.ts`
- [x] T15.6 Add integration tests in `backend/src/api/rooms.test.ts`
  - [x] Correct guess increments score by 100 (case-insensitive)
  - [x] Incorrect guess adds 0
  - [x] Empty/whitespace guess returns 400
  - [x] Guess history is visible to all participants after polling

### Phase 16: Frontend — State & API Client
- [x] T16.1 Add `Guess` type and update `RoomSnapshot` in `frontend/src/services/api.ts`
- [x] T16.2 Add `submitGuess(code, participantId, guess)` to `frontend/src/services/api.ts`
- [x] T16.3 Add `submitGuess(text)` to `RoomStore` in `frontend/src/state/roomStore.ts`

### Phase 17: Frontend — UI Implementation
- [x] T17.1 `GuessForm.tsx`: Connect to store; validate non-empty before calling API; show inline error
- [x] T17.2 `GuessForm.tsx`: Disable/hide for the drawer with an explanatory message
- [x] T17.3 `ResultPanel.tsx`: Render the full guess history from `room.guesses`
- [x] T17.4 `Scoreboard.tsx`: Render per-participant scores sorted highest-first from `room.scores`
- [x] T17.5 `GamePage.tsx`: Show "Clear Canvas" button for the drawer (client-side state reset only)

